# motion-state

Every `/studio` project carries a `state.json` that is the **source of truth**. `scene.js` is generated from it (`node scripts/state-to-scene.mjs`).

Schema lives in `skills/motion-state/schema.json` (JSON Schema draft-07). Runtime lives in `skills/motion-state/runtime.mjs`:

```
validate(state);         // throws on schema or anti-slop violation
at(state, t);            // → beats overlapping t
add(state, beat);        // returns new state with beat appended
remove(state, beatId);   // returns new state with beat removed
update(state, id, patch) // returns new state with patched beat
summary(state);          // → { beatCount, layerCount, duration, primitives }
```

Browser surface: `window.__studio.state` mirrors the same API. Mutations trigger `rebuild()` so GSDevTools reflects the change live.

**Anti-slop Group S** (enforced at every mutation):
- S1: `at` in `[0, duration]`
- S2: layer overlap without `allowOverlap: true`
- S4: missing `schemaVersion`
- S5: `beats.length > 200` (LLM runaway guard)

For the full contract, schema, and limitations: see `skills/motion-state/SKILL.md`.